## FINAL
**REJECT** 2.9 wave-2 walker vs guard parity on nested-paren shapes.
Stmt `println` **does** miss shapes that free-call `eprintln` catches:
any SECRET IDENT that appears **after a nested `RPAREN` still inside
the same sink argument**. Live emit-c prints `tok` (or drops the
secret expr). The eprintln guard refuses the same source. Wave-2
later-arg smoke is not a substitute for this rail. WT check `depth`
is not in the 07:49 ELF and would not give stmt `println` the guard.

Fix (not this worker): stop special-casing stmt `println`, **or** give
`c_emit_println` a depth-aware scan / `c_secret_emit_guard` on joined
arg text; **and** ship a host that actually runs the depth-aware
check walker (or check stays FN).

